('DT-C01-L01','Day Trading: What It Is and What It Is Not — The defining boundary','DAY_TRADING_BOOK_1',1,null,null,null,'supplemental',true,true,false,'site-lab.html?lab=DT-C01-L01',40001,'{"track":"book","source_kind":"book_plus_research","source_ref":"Day Trading Chapter 1","chapter_title":"Day Trading: What It Is and What It Is Not","skill_group":"Day Trading","mode":"recognition","difficulty":"beginner","what":"This lab isolates the Chapter 1 skill ''The defining boundary'' from the broader day-trading workflow so you can name the evidence before judging the outcome.","why":"The defining boundary matters because it changes what evidence is relevant, how risk is bounded, and whether an intraday idea is actionable or should remain an observation.","when":"Use this lab when practicing Chapter 1 decisions involving the defining boundary, especially before converting a scanner hit, chart pattern, or market event into a trade plan.","objective":"Correctly recognize and use the defining boundary without hindsight, then explain how it changes the next trading decision.","how":["Read the Chapter 1 section on “The defining boundary” and write a one-sentence definition in your own words.","Freeze the historical clock or worksheet before the decision point. Record only information that would have been available then.","List the observable evidence, the inference you are considering, and the invalidation or reason to pass.","Classify the condition without predicting what happens next. State what would have to change before your classification changes.","Reveal the next segment or compare the completed worksheet, then score the decision process separately from the later outcome."],"questions":["What is directly observable about the defining boundary at the decision point?","Why does this evidence matter here, and what does it *not* prove?","When would you use this information, and when would you refuse to rely on it?","What is the next action: ENTER, WATCH, or NO TRADE, and what evidence/invalidation supports that choice?"],"data_requirement":"Use the chapter workflow and only the market/account data explicitly required by the exercise.","historical_anchor":null,"source_urls":[],"research_provenance":"Derived from the uploaded Day Trading book; historical anchors and market-mechanics details were cross-checked with current official web sources and stock-market data tools during the v0.13.3 build.","tags":["chapter-1","recognition","the-defining-boundary"]}'::jsonb),
