('TAPE-C01-L01','What Tape Reading Is - and What It Is Not — Start with evidence, not a story','READING_THE_TAPE',1,null,null,null,'supplemental',true,true,false,'site-lab.html?lab=TAPE-C01-L01',50001,'{"track":"book","source_kind":"book_plus_research","source_ref":"Reading the Tape Chapter 1","chapter_title":"What Tape Reading Is - and What It Is Not","skill_group":"Tape Reading","mode":"observation","difficulty":"beginner","what":"This lab isolates the tape-reading evidence problem ''Start with evidence, not a story'' and requires you to separate displayed facts from inference.","why":"Start with evidence, not a story matters because tape reading is useful only when the observation, feed limitation, and inference are kept distinct.","when":"Use this lab while practicing Chapter 1, particularly when a fast market tempts you to explain participant intent from incomplete quote, trade, or depth information.","objective":"Read start with evidence, not a story from the available evidence without mind reading, hindsight, or unsupported certainty.","how":["Review the Chapter 1 section on “Start with evidence, not a story” and identify exactly which fields are observable.","Record the quote/depth/tape sequence with timestamps or sequence order. Preserve unknown or ambiguous classifications.","Write two columns: OBSERVATION and INFERENCE. Do not move a statement into the observation column unless the feed directly supports it.","Classify the displayed evidence only; do not predict direction and do not infer hidden identity or motive.","Review the result without rewriting the original observation after seeing what happened next."],"questions":["What did the feed actually show about start with evidence, not a story?","Which statement is inference rather than directly observed fact?","When is this evidence useful, and what context must be present before it affects a decision?","What would make you downgrade the signal, wait, or choose NO TRADE?"],"data_requirement":"Live or simulated quote/Time & Sales observation is preferred. Record only fields actually displayed by the chosen feed.","historical_anchor":null,"source_urls":[],"research_provenance":"Derived from the uploaded Reading the Tape book; market-mechanics constraints were cross-checked with current official exchange/regulatory sources and stock-market research tools during the v0.13.3 build.","tags":["chapter-1","observation","start-with-evidence-not-a-story"],"historical_tape_warning":"Historical candles do not reconstruct historical Level II or Time & Sales. Use live, recorded, or simulated order-flow data for tape-specific evidence."}'::jsonb),
