insert into public.commons_topics
(forum_code,author_user_id,author_label,title,body,status,is_pinned,is_locked,is_official,legacy_source_code,reply_count,view_count,last_post_at)
values ('START_HERE',null,'Official Platform Guide','Start Here: What, Why, When, and How to Use Every Platform Tool','## PURPOSE
The platform is designed as a learning workflow, not a collection of disconnected pages. Use the tools in the order required by the question you are trying to answer.

## QUICK TOOL MAP
### Platform Navigation & Dashboard
WHAT: Use the member Dashboard as the operating hub for learning, access, settings, support, billing, and activity.
WHEN: Use it when you need to resume work, verify access, or change account-level settings.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open dashboard.html, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### Book Access & Lab Registry
WHAT: Use book access and the Lab Registry to move from a book concept into structured practice without changing locked book content.
WHEN: Use it after reading a chapter or when you want to practice a specific skill by book.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open labs.html, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### No-Look-Ahead Historical Replay
WHAT: Practice historical decisions using only information available at the simulated decision point.
WHEN: Use it when training entries, exits, structure, catalyst interpretation, or trade management.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open simulator.html, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### Advanced Market Simulator & Replay
WHAT: Use replay and simulated execution to practice timing, entries, exits, and management without live capital risk.
WHEN: Use it after you can state a setup, trigger, invalidation, and risk boundary.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open simulator.html, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### Trading Journal & Performance Analytics
WHAT: Record the plan, actual decisions, MFE/MAE, process adherence, and review outcomes.
WHEN: Use it after observation, paper, simulator, or live decisions that are worth learning from.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open journal.html, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### Market Tutor
WHAT: Use the Tutor to explain concepts, question your reasoning, and help connect evidence to the curriculum.
WHEN: Use it when a concept is unclear or you need guided review rather than a trade signal.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open market-tutor.html, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### Market Discovery Lab
WHAT: Build an eligible universe and identify candidates that deserve research rather than treating scanner output as permission to trade.
WHEN: Use it before watchlist construction and whenever market conditions change the active universe.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open advanced-tool.html?tool=DISCOVERY_LAB, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### Scanner Builder & Historical Scanner Replay
WHAT: Design, test, and replay scanner logic so filters match the strategy and market regime.
WHEN: Use it when you need repeatable discovery rules or want to test why a candidate appeared.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open advanced-tool.html?tool=SCANNER_BUILDER, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### Watchlist & Trade-Plan Workbench
WHAT: Turn researched candidates into ranked, conditional plans with levels, triggers, invalidation, and cancellation conditions.
WHEN: Use it after discovery/catalyst checks and before the active trading window.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open advanced-tool.html?tool=WATCHLIST_WORKBENCH, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### Catalyst & Filing Research Lab
WHAT: Verify why a stock is moving using primary sources, timestamps, filings, and reliable news.
WHEN: Use it before relying on a catalyst or explaining unusual price/volume activity.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open advanced-tool.html?tool=CATALYST_RESEARCH, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### Float & Supply Lab
WHAT: Study float, shares outstanding, offerings, warrants, convertibles, and other supply conditions that can affect tradeability.
WHEN: Use it when evaluating small-cap momentum, dilution risk, or unusual turnover.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open advanced-tool.html?tool=FLOAT_SUPPLY_LAB, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### Market Structure Lab
WHAT: Classify trend, range, swing structure, levels, and changing market character before choosing a setup.
WHEN: Use it before entries and whenever price stops behaving like the original thesis.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open advanced-tool.html?tool=MARKET_STRUCTURE_LAB, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### Multi-Timeframe Synchronizer
WHAT: Assign each timeframe a job and reconcile higher-timeframe context with lower-timeframe execution.
WHEN: Use it when a fast chart conflicts with the broader structure or a setup looks different across 1m/3m/5m/daily views.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open advanced-tool.html?tool=MULTI_TIMEFRAME, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### Risk & Position Sizing Laboratory
WHAT: Translate invalidation distance and risk budget into a position size before entry.
WHEN: Use it before every simulated or live trade plan.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open advanced-tool.html?tool=RISK_POSITION_LAB, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### Execution Laboratory
WHAT: Practice order selection, entry control, partial fills, slippage, and implementation quality.
WHEN: Use it when spread, liquidity, speed, or order type can materially change the planned risk.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open advanced-tool.html?tool=EXECUTION_LAB, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### Liquidity & Spread Laboratory
WHAT: Measure bid/ask spread, displayed liquidity, trading activity, and exit feasibility.
WHEN: Use it before committing size or trading thin/fast names.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open advanced-tool.html?tool=LIQUIDITY_SPREAD_LAB, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### Order Flow & Tape Laboratory
WHAT: Practice quote, Time & Sales, Level II, pace, absorption, and liquidity evidence while separating observation from inference.
WHEN: Use it when order-flow evidence is available and the chart context gives it meaning.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open advanced-tool.html?tool=ORDER_FLOW_TAPE_LAB, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### Strategy Validation
WHAT: Test a defined strategy on clean samples with frozen rules, consistent metrics, and failure classifications.
WHEN: Use it after the strategy rules are explicit enough to test repeatedly.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open advanced-tool.html?tool=STRATEGY_VALIDATION, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### News & Source Verification
WHAT: Build a source hierarchy and separate verified facts, attributed claims, inference, and unresolved information.
WHEN: Use it whenever news or social discussion is affecting a candidate.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open advanced-tool.html?tool=CATALYST_RESEARCH, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### Corporate Actions & Adjustments
WHAT: Understand splits, reverse splits, dividends, mergers, symbol changes, and chart-adjustment effects.
WHEN: Use it when a historical chart or security terms look inconsistent across dates or platforms.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open advanced-tool.html?tool=CATALYST_RESEARCH, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### Extended-Hours Context
WHAT: Evaluate premarket and after-hours movement with explicit liquidity, spread, volatility, and news-risk awareness.
WHEN: Use it when a setup develops outside the regular session or the prior close no longer reflects current information.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open simulator.html, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### Halts & Limit Up-Limit Down
WHAT: Recognize when volatility controls or other halts change execution, liquidity, and price discovery.
WHEN: Use it during extreme moves or when trading pauses interrupt the normal continuous market.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open simulator.html, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### Opening, Closing & Reopening Auctions
WHAT: Study auction-driven price discovery and the difference between continuous trading and auction matching.
WHEN: Use it around the open, close, and post-halt reopenings.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open advanced-tool.html?tool=MARKET_STRUCTURE_LAB, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### Order Types & Execution Control
WHAT: Choose market, limit, stop, stop-limit, and timing instructions based on the actual execution objective and risk.
WHEN: Use it when translating a trade plan into an executable order.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open advanced-tool.html?tool=EXECUTION_LAB, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

### Trade Review & Analytics
WHAT: Review decisions, mistakes, adherence, MFE/MAE, and repeated patterns across clean samples.
WHEN: Use it after enough observations exist to compare process rather than one outcome.
WHY: It makes that part of the decision explicit and reviewable.
HOW: Open dashboard.html?tab=activity, define the question first, record the evidence, and pass the result to the next appropriate workflow.

## DEFAULT LEARNING SEQUENCE
1. Learn the concept in the book or Learning System.
2. Practice it in a Lab without looking ahead.
3. Use research tools only for the evidence they are designed to provide.
4. Use the Simulator for execution and management practice.
5. Save the reasoning and result in the Journal.
6. Review process quality and repeated errors before changing a rule.

## WHEN TO STOP
If required data is missing, the spread/liquidity makes execution unreasonable, the catalyst cannot be verified, the invalidation cannot be defined, or the setup never triggers, NO TRADE is a valid outcome.','published',true,false,true,'V0133_MASTER_TOOL_GUIDE',0,0,now())
